ding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, for each required narrative topic (observability exception, subprocess limitations, behavior deltas, native refresh), whether its text is derived from a named source or carried as generator-owned template prose, so the byte-current drift gate has a coherent contract for those sections.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'sourcing the schema + ownership/secret-name registries' and 'covers every ... observability-exception, subprocess-limitation, and behavior-delta topic named in the epic'","The named sources (_config_schema.py, check_config_ownership.py ownership map, rebar._child_env secret names) carry config keys/owners/secret names, not narrative prose for observability exceptions, subprocess limitations, or behavior deltas — so that content must be hardcoded template text in the generator, which the plan does not state","ABSENCE: no statement of the data source for the non-schema narrative topics means an implementer cannot tell whether these sections are generated-from-data or author-maintained template prose, which affects whether the byte-drift gate is meaningful for them"],"finding":"The generated reference is required to cover topics (obse